          "Defend property tax management and local government efficiency — a homeowner-dominant district (86.3%) with $96,169 income expects government to deliver services at reasonable cost; transparency on how property tax dollars are spent and visible results on infrastructure and services maintenance are the unglamorous governance work that keeps suburban Republicans aligned.",
          "Do not treat 69% as a permanent majority — the 31% Democratic share in a college-educated, affluent district is higher than the raw demographic profile would predict and reflects a genuinely persuadable constituency on quality-of-life issues; any incumbent who campaigns this seat as safe rather than defended risks allowing a credible challenger to gain traction on specific governance failures."
