          "Engage the 26.2% renter constituency with specific attention to housing affordability and service-access concerns: while renters are minority, they represent roughly 3,800-4,200 households whose material concerns are real and whose vote is available if opposition candidates address their priorities and the incumbent does not.",
          "Avoid defaulting to cultural messaging in place of constituent service: the 21.7% college attainment and $69,554 income signal a constituency that evaluates primarily on household economic concerns — abstract partisan rhetoric is electorally valuable only if it accompanies concrete answers to property tax burden, service costs, and economic security."
