          "Lead with homeowner economic security and property governance: the 53% result in a 79%-homeowner district suggests the incumbent has addressed specific concerns—property tax fairness, rural infrastructure, or local service sustainability—with enough credibility to retain a slice of the homeowner base despite structural Republican advantage. Maintain and expand this engagement through concrete legislative outcomes, not abstract positioning.",
          "Engage the ~34% renter constituency and younger adults as a core coalition partner: renters and younger households are the demographic base most likely to have shifted the 2024 result toward Democrats and are the population most responsive to messaging on housing affordability, student debt, and economic opportunity. This is not a secondary constituency; it is essential to the 53% margin.",
          "Avoid treating 53% as a stable floor: in a rural district this competitive, a margin of six points is mathematically vulnerable to any significant shift in turnout, demographic mobilization among the ~8% gap, or erosion of homeowner support through economic anxiety or specific policy failure. This seat requires active constituent engagement and concrete delivery, not passive reliance on the 2024 result."
