          { name: "Neglecting the ~6% Demographic Gap & Newer-Arrival Communities", tag: "avoid", why: "The ~6% gap in reported Census categories likely represents Hispanic, Asian, and other immigrant and newer-arrival communities whose economic profile may include skilled professionals and entrepreneurs but whose civic and political integration into the Republican coalition appears incomplete. Treating this population as demographically irrelevant or assuming they will default to either party is a strategic error in a district where 6% represents the difference between 56% and a genuinely competitive result. These communities are often persuadable on education, healthcare access, and economic opportunity if they perceive authentic engagement rather than tokenism." }
