          "Lead with housing and rental affordability: more than one-third of the district rents rather than owns, making housing costs and access to homeownership a direct quality-of-life concern; this is the constituency most likely to constitute the 48% opposition and most responsive to concrete policy on housing policy and affordability.",
          "Engage the college-educated professional constituency specifically on healthcare costs and economic mobility: 30.2% college attainment in a $78,932-median-income district suggests educated professionals whose career advancement and family economic security are contingent on healthcare access, student loan management, and whether the district's schools and services support professional-class quality of life.",
