          { name: "Assuming Partisan Loyalty Negates the Need for Active Community Engagement", tag: "avoid", why: "At $51,317 median income with 53.5% renters and a young demographic (34.0 median age), MO-HD-26 constituents evaluate their representative on material delivery — whether housing is affordable, whether jobs are available and pay well, whether healthcare is accessible — not on partisan identity alone. An incumbent whose campaign consists of partisan messaging and voter mobilization without concrete constituent engagement on these economic issues is assuming that Democratic registration equals infinite electoral patience; in a working-class community this tight economically, that assumption is strategically dangerous and can be exploited by a challenger who focuses on specific material concerns." }
