          "Consolidate working-class homeowner support by focusing on job quality, wage sustainability, and small-business vitality in a $64,845-median-income district where household economic security depends on stable local employment rather than credential-based professional advancement.",
          "Engage Black and Hispanic communities with specific constituent attention on economic mobility, healthcare access, and whether district economic recovery is reaching these populations at parity with white households—avoiding the assumption that a 56% margin means proportional support across all demographic groups.",
