          "Engage the 22.1% renter constituency specifically on tenant protections, zoning reform, and housing cost; renters represent approximately one-fifth of the district and may evaluate differently than homeowners, and their concerns often receive minimal legislative attention in suburban majority-homeowner districts.",
          "Investigate and address the 4.5% demographic gap—whether it represents American Indian, immigrant, or multiracial constituents—and ensure legislative responsiveness; unopposed governance can leave emerging constituencies invisible, and their mobilization by a challenger could rapidly alter district competitiveness."
