          "Consolidate African American Democratic base while actively engaging white working-class swing voters: the 27.41% Black population is the electoral foundation of a 62% Democratic result, but the 51.28% white population contains the marginal swing voters who will determine whether the margin holds or contracts; neither group can be taken for granted.",
          "Lead with concrete household economic improvement: the $58,875 median income and 37.7-year median age indicate a constituency of working adults whose primary question is whether their situation is getting better or worse; economic messaging must be grounded in specific programs (minimum wage, healthcare cost relief, childcare support, job training) rather than partisan positioning.",
