          "Build specific, ongoing relationships with the Black community leadership and civic infrastructure; at 39.55%, African American residents are the largest demographic group and their economic mobility concerns around homeownership, workforce development, and educational access require targeted legislative attention rather than generic coalition management.",
          "Understand the white working-class realignment in 2024: whether through Democratic voting, low turnout, or failed Republican recruitment, the 46.64% white plurality's electoral behavior shifted; do not assume this is permanent without building explicit constituent engagement around material economic concerns like wages, healthcare costs, and job quality.",
          "Treat unopposed status as a strategic window, not permanent security: 100% in a single cycle is a campaign snapshot, not a durable coalition signal in a district with this level of demographic and economic diversity; use the window to build infrastructure before the next Republican recruitment challenge emerges."
