          { name: "Treating the Demographic Gap as Irrelevant", tag: "avoid", why: "The 4.79% unaccounted-for population in a district with likely Native American communities creates a governance obligation that does not disappear because the partisan margin is safe. Communities that are invisible in Census data are often invisible in constituent service, policy attention, and institutional engagement — and that invisibility accumulates into alienation and reduced civic participation. A representative who ignores the demographic gap in favor of focusing only on the consolidated Republican base is governing less than the full district and is missing an opportunity to build the inclusive constituent relationships that make supermajorities genuinely durable." }
