          "Activate the college-educated female voters and dual-income households that likely dominate the professional base: at 57.8% college education and $89,761 median income, this district includes significant numbers of educated women in professional occupations whose economic security concerns include healthcare access, workplace equity, and reproductive autonomy. These voters are less persuadable by abstract progressive messaging than by specific policy delivery and evidence that the incumbent is attending to their material interests.",
