          { name: "Treating 73% as a Ceiling Rather Than a Floor", tag: "avoid", why: "A 73% result in a deeply red state against a Democratic opponent means Republican consolidation of the base, but it does not guarantee immunity from a more compelling Republican primary challenger who can articulate the district's material economic concerns more effectively. The risk to Thompson is not a Democratic flip but an intra-party primary challenge from a candidate who speaks more directly to business-owner and skilled-trades constituencies' specific legislative interests. Complacency about the 73% as a permanent achievement is the primary vulnerability." },
          { name: "Constructing a Governing Agenda Around Abstract Conservative Ideology", tag: "avoid", why: "A district with 18.7% college attainment — the lowest in this sequence — is less likely to engage with abstract ideological arguments and more likely to evaluate representatives on direct economic impact and practical problem-solving. A governing agenda constructed around general conservative principles without connection to the specific regulatory, tax, and workforce concerns of business owners and skilled trades in Mo-HD-53 fails to match the constituency's actual decision-making framework. Ideological messaging should be secondary to demonstrable legislative delivery on the material interests that sustain the 73% margin." }
