          "Address the college-attainment gap strategically: at 18.7%, this district has fewer college-educated voters and more working-class wealth than typical Republican strongholds, which means messaging should emphasize practical economic competence and direct constituent service over abstract conservative principles that may not resonate as strongly with non-degreed business and trades constituencies.",
          "Maintain awareness that the 3.16% Hispanic and ~4% AIAN populations, while small, represent constituencies whose economic concerns and community standing can shift over time if underserved; specific attention to workforce development and small-business access for these communities prevents a small demographic from becoming a latent opposition source.",
          "Treat the 27% Democratic opposition not as a threat to the 73% but as a data point about what portion of the constituency may be persuadable on specific economic issues; a Republican incumbent's job in a 73-27 district is not winning back opposition voters but ensuring that the consolidation of the 73% is not vulnerable to a more compelling Republican primary challenger."
