          "Address property tax fairness and healthcare cost management directly for the 65.3% homeowner majority; at $67,044 income, fixed costs are rising faster than income growth, and a legislative agenda focused on property tax relief and Medicare/healthcare sustainability is the material concern of this older, asset-holding constituency.",
          "Ensure visible engagement with Hispanic, Black, and Asian residents across the district—the 5.22% demographic gap combined with the absence of these communities from partisan narrative creates an invisibility problem, and specific constituent service and legislative attention to their economic mobility concerns prevents future electoral drift.",
          "Build a distinct legislative identity around cost-of-living issues rather than relying on the 70% margin as a passive resource; property tax policy, healthcare affordability, housing, and wages are the issues that bind together the economically diverse constituency within the Republican-leaning base and preempt a credible challenger's ability to mobilize the 30% opposition plus disaffected majority voters."
