          { name: "Partisan Ideology and National Party Messaging", tag: "avoid", why: "An 8-point Republican victory in a district with moderate income and education levels suggests voters are pragmatic and not ideologically locked. Relying on national party talking points or abstract ideological battles will fail to move undecided voters focused on local pocketbook issues. Candidate-specific, district-focused messaging will consistently outperform messaging tied to broader partisan movements." }
