          { name: "Generic Partisan Messaging as a Substitute for Economic Solutions", tag: "avoid", why: "In a low-diversity, economically stressed rural district, voters evaluate representatives primarily on whether they are materially improving constituent quality of life. Abstract conservative positioning, partisan attacks, or cultural messaging that does not address healthcare costs, employment opportunity, or service viability will fail to generate the constituent loyalty necessary to maintain the current Republican advantage if a challenger emerges with specific economic solutions. This district requires a representative whose legislative work demonstrates concrete commitment to rural economic security." }
