          { name: "Assuming Homeowner Consensus Across Income & Tenure Differences", tag: "avoid", why: "While 77.7% of Mo-HD-59 is owner-occupied, homeowners in this affluent, educated district have diverse interests: younger first-time buyers concerned with affordability, established families focused on school quality, and older empty-nesters prioritizing tax stability. Treating homeowners as a monolithic constituency risks missing the material divisions among them — divisions that a skilled Democratic challenger can exploit by emphasizing education quality and affordability for younger households while reassuring older voters on fiscal responsibility. The incumbent's homeowner base is real but not undifferentiated; specific constituent engagement across these tenure and age segments is required." }
