          "Engage the Black community with specificity on healthcare equity, criminal justice outcomes, and economic opportunity — the 35.16% plurality is the foundation of the Democratic supermajority, and their evaluation of whether the representative is materially improving access and outcomes, not just advocating symbolically, determines whether the 79% holds or erodes.",
          "Address the 21% Republican share as a genuine constituency rather than dismissing it: understand what drives Republican voters in a 35% Black, 39.2% renter, $57,893-income district and whether they represent persuadable swing voters frustrated by specific policy failures or simply the ideological base; if persuadable, target them on economic competence and material delivery rather than expecting them to shift parties.",
          "Build a continuous accountability mechanism with the renter and working-class constituencies: housing stability, wage adequacy, and healthcare access are not one-time campaign promises but ongoing governance metrics that constituents evaluate regularly; representatives who report progress on these measures maintain higher margins and stronger turnout than those who default to partisan rhetoric."
