          "Build active relationships with neighborhood organizations, schools, and service providers: unopposed status provides the opportunity to deepen constituency engagement without electoral pressure — using this window to build visible, ongoing relationships with community institutions and to demonstrate responsiveness to school-funding, healthcare-access, and police-accountability concerns is the most durable insurance against future challenge.",
          "Do not assume unopposed status equals invulnerability: a 62% Black, $46K-income, 49%-renter district is politically aligned but economically pressured — if service delivery fails, if an alternative emerges that speaks more credibly to housing stability or workforce opportunity, or if an organized constituency mobilization occurs around specific unmet needs, the absence of a 2024 challenger provides no structural protection against a future credible challenge."
