          "Lead with renter economic security and housing affordability as the primary constituent concern — the 65.3% renter rate is among the highest in the state, and at $47,178 median income, housing costs consume a material share of household budgets. Affordable housing policy, tenant protection, wage-level employment, and healthcare access are the issues that activate voter participation in a constituency this economically constrained.",
          "Build and maintain active constituent engagement infrastructure even in unopposed cycles — town halls, neighborhood canvassing, direct renter household outreach, and demonstrated responsiveness to service requests are the difference between an incumbent who can weather a credible challenger and one who loses after years of assuming the seat is safe.",
