          "Address the working-class economic agenda directly: job quality, wage standards, healthcare access, and childcare costs matter more to a $54,462-median-income constituency than abstract messaging; the 16% Republican opposition includes working adults who are not unreachable but unconvinced current policy is helping them.",
          "Leverage the 38% college-attainment rate and younger median age (36.3) as indicators of a constituency that responds to specific policy detail and outcome metrics rather than partisan generics; demonstrate concrete delivery on education funding, student debt, and entry-level job creation."
