          { name: "Treating 74% as a Safe Supermajority", tag: "avoid", why: "A 74% result in a college-educated, upper-middle-income district is not a landslide that permits passive governance—it is a supermajority held by alignment between the incumbent and an educated constituency that evaluates on competence and material outcomes. If the incumbent takes this coalition for granted, fails to articulate why Democratic governance is delivering for college-educated homeowners, or allows a credible challenger to reposition on tax fairness or school choice, the supermajority can erode to a plurality or loss in a single cycle. This district requires active constituent engagement and clear messaging about why Democrats are superior on the issues that matter most to upper-middle-income professionals." }
