          "Consolidate college-educated suburban voters as the base: the 51.5% college attainment is the district's dominant demographic story, and this group has become electorally volatile nationally when they perceive either party as indifferent to their economic interests or professional concerns. Messaging must speak to what college-educated, affluent homeowners actually care about: fiscal stewardship, school quality, property values, and government efficacy.",
          "Engage Asian and Hispanic professional and entrepreneurial communities with specificity: the 3.23% Asian and 5.16% Hispanic populations are small but concentrated enough that modest shifts in their support swing a 60-40 seat. Focus on economic opportunity, professional licensing, business development support, and institutional access — not on demographic outreach alone.",
