          "Lead on high-income homeowner economic concerns: property tax fairness, school funding that preserves neighborhood quality, infrastructure investment, and cost-of-living management at the upper-middle-class level are the material concerns of a $100k-income, 62% college-educated, 71% homeowner constituency. Doll's visibility on these issues — particularly in comparison to what a Republican challenger might offer — is the primary driver of seat durability.",
          "Build authentic engagement with the 7.9% demographic gap and the Black (7.4%) and Hispanic (5.15%) communities: in an affluent, highly educated district where white homeowners are the numerical majority, it is easy for other constituencies to become invisible. Specific constituent attention to Black and Hispanic households' economic mobility concerns, educational outcomes in their communities, and healthcare access is both governing obligation and electoral insurance against the assumption that affluence equals monolithic Democratic support.",
          "Anticipate that Republicans may target this seat in 2026 or 2028 with a candidate positioned as a tax-conscious fiscal conservative who respects school quality and property values: unopposed status is not a prediction of future outcomes in an affluent suburban district. Build legislative record, constituent service visibility, and donor relationships now that will be hard to dislodge when a credible challenger emerges."
