          { name: "Ideological Positioning Over Suburban Material Concerns", tag: "avoid", why: "A constituency at $79,290 income with 25.8% college attainment does not organize around abstract ideological principles—it organizes around school funding, property tax fairness, infrastructure investment, and whether government competence is evident in daily life. Any campaign that prioritizes ideological purity or cultural issues over the material governance concerns of affluent suburbanites will fail to consolidate the base and will invite a challenger to run as the fiscal-competence, education-focused alternative. This district rewards candidates who translate conservative fiscal philosophy into specific outcomes that matter to homeowners and families." }
