          { name: "Assuming the Incumbent's 52% is a Durable Coalition", tag: "avoid", why: "A 4-point margin in a district this affluent and educated is a warning signal, not a victory lap. College-educated voters with $90,663 income are financially secure enough to split tickets and shift support based on performance and competence. An incumbent who treats 52% as permission to pursue a more partisan or ideological legislative agenda — rather than as a mandate to govern with visible competence and deliver on the fiscal and education issues that matter to swing voters — will find that coalition more vulnerable in the next cycle." }
