          "Engage college-educated voters directly on education policy: 73.5% college attainment signals a constituency whose children attend competitive public and private schools, and whose economic mobility depends on educational excellence. School funding adequacy, teacher quality, and competition with suburban districts in neighboring states for talent are the real education issues here, not culture-war framing.",
          "Address healthcare access and cost specifically for the 46.9-year-old, $152,890-income demographic: this is a population entering peak healthcare utilization years with the resources to seek care outside the state if Missouri's healthcare system fails them. Healthcare quality, specialist access, and cost transparency in the state's major metro areas are the specific concerns that determine whether this constituency stays engaged.",
          "Monitor and directly counter any Democratic messaging about fiscal recklessness or underfunded core services: at 55%, Keathley is holding this seat despite a demographic profile that should produce 62-63% Republican margins — meaning 7-8 points of high-income suburban voters are either genuinely persuadable or are voting against him specifically. If Democratic opposition successfully frames Republican governance as fiscally incompetent or hostile to public investment in education and infrastructure, the margin will erode rapidly."
