          "The 47% opposition in a district this educated and this suburban is not a residual minority — it is a coalition of voters who made an active choice to support an alternative. Understanding whether that 47% is concentrated among renters frustrated by housing costs and education funding, among college-educated professionals concerned about healthcare or environmental governance, or both, is the single most important analytical task for any candidate seeking to hold or win this seat. Wellenkamp's 53% is a floor to defend against erosion, not a ceiling to build from. In a district where 43.9% have college degrees and the median age is 35, a narrow Republican hold requires active engagement with the specific concerns that drove 47% of voters to the opposition — whether that means addressing education funding, healthcare access, housing affordability, or all three. Any candidate who campaigns this seat as though 53% represents comfortable Republican terrain will find that assumption disproven in the next competitive cycle.",
