          "Lead with working-family economic security: cost-of-living pressures, reliable employment, healthcare access, and K-12 education quality are the direct household concerns for a $55,039 median income constituency with 41.9% renters and 33% college attainment — framing around abstract conservative principles will not resonate as effectively as specific solutions to material household problems.",
          "Engage the 5.5% demographic gap and all minority constituencies with deliberate specificity: while no single non-white community is large enough to swing the seat in isolation, collective neglect of the 8.86% non-white plus 5.5% gap populations sends a clear signal about representation and opens a pathway for challenger investment if a credible alternative emerges.",
          "Build a persistent local presence and constituent service infrastructure: the 73% margin likely reflects a degree of incumbent advantage and name recognition rather than a structural Republican supermajority, which means sustained constituent attention and responsiveness to district problems is the most reliable way to maintain the seat in a competitive cycle."
