          { name: "Minority Community Invisibility in Strategic Messaging", tag: "avoid", why: "With 85.16% white population, HD-136 permits a strategy focused entirely on white working and professional class voters—but the 4.89% Hispanic, 3.13% Black, and 2.57% Asian residents represent real constituents whose economic and social concerns (wage work, healthcare access, educational opportunity) can become invisible when strategic messaging targets only the white renter-college-educated majority. This invisibility is both a governance failure and a missed opportunity to build deeper support among minority communities whose turnout and persuadability can shift close margins." }
