          { name: "Partisan Messaging Over Constituent Problem-Solving", tag: "avoid", why: "MO-HD-138 is a deeply red district where partisan advantage is structural, but that advantage does not insulate an incumbent from losing if constituents believe the legislator is not solving their material problems. A 49.6-year-old voter concerned about healthcare costs and property taxes will not support a legislator based on party alone if an alternative candidate can demonstrate concrete solutions to those problems. Any campaign that relies on partisan messaging rather than on documented constituent service and district-specific legislative accomplishment risks underestimating a challenger who leads with local problem-solving and evidence of listening." }
