          { name: "Ignoring Renter & Non-Homeowner Constituencies", tag: "avoid", why: "With a 19.4% renter rate and 42-year median age, Mo-HD-141 includes renters, younger adults, and working families whose economic concerns (housing affordability, wage growth, healthcare access) may not align perfectly with the homeowner-centric agenda. An incumbent who campaigns primarily to the 80.6% homeowner majority and does not actively engage renters and younger working adults risks losing their participation and creating an opening for a challenger who speaks to their distinct economic needs. Renters in a district this rural often have specific economic frustrations that deserve attention rather than assumption." }
