          "Address the 17.3% college attainment gap as a workforce development issue, not an education abstraction: community college funding, vocational training partnerships, and pathways from secondary education into skilled trades are material concerns for a district where educational access constrains economic mobility.",
          "Serve the 26.9% renter population explicitly: housing affordability, tenant protections, and the relationship between wage growth and housing costs are the daily economic reality for a quarter of the district, and their interests can diverge from homeowner priorities on zoning, property tax policy, and housing development.",
