          { name: "Partisan Culture-War Messaging as Primary Campaign Strategy", tag: "avoid", why: "A 12.9% college-attainment constituency is less responsive to partisan culture-war framing than to concrete local governance performance. Defaulting to abstract conservative messaging rather than addressing the material economic security concerns of a median-income, renter-inclusive, low-education-attainment district risks creating the perception that the incumbent is addressing national partisan concerns rather than local constituent needs—a perception that, over time, can activate opposition in a constituency that should be electorally safe." }
