          { name: "Cultural Grievance Framing Over Economic Delivery", tag: "avoid", why: "MO-HD-160's Republican alignment is fundamentally economic and practical — working-class homeowners concerned with taxes, healthcare costs, and whether government delivers basic services — not primarily cultural. Any candidate who leads with cultural or partisan grievance messaging rather than concrete answers to healthcare affordability, property tax fairness, or rural infrastructure viability will misread this constituency's priorities and leave political space for an opponent who takes their material concerns seriously. The 78% result is robust only as long as the Republican candidate is seen as delivering for working people; pure cultural messaging cannot sustain a margin this large in a district where economic anxiety is real." }
