          "Lead with rural economic and infrastructure specifics: property tax fairness, rural broadband deployment, agricultural support, and rural healthcare investment are the material governance concerns for a 42.6-year-old, 74.6% homeowner, working-class constituency at $65,454 income. Messaging must be concrete and locally grounded, not abstract ideological positioning.",
          "Engage the college-attainment gap strategically: at 27.6%, this district is below state average and at the threshold where educational polarization becomes durable. However, rural voters without college degrees are not ideologically frozen — they evaluate based on whether government is delivering results for them. Any candidate must address this constituency's material concerns in language that reflects respect for their experience and judgment, not condescension or abstract values messaging.",
