          "The 25% opposition is distributed across ideological conservatives and economic libertarians unlikely to be persuaded by messaging; the marginal vote is within the Democratic base through mobilization, not recruitment from the opposition.",
          "With 50.6% college attainment and 51.5% renter rate, housing affordability, education investment, and workplace protections are the material governance issues that sustain the Democratic alignment—these are not optional messaging priorities.",
          "The racial diversity (39.61% non-white population) means that Black, Hispanic, and Asian community specific concerns—economic mobility, healthcare access, immigration and labor policy, education equity—require targeted constituent attention beyond generic Democratic messaging; these communities delivered the margin and expect service."
