          "Do not assume 58% is a comfortable floor: in a working-class district this economically stressed, partisan loyalty is conditional on whether government is perceived as delivering material benefit. A Democratic candidate who focuses on household economics rather than cultural positioning, and who avoids alienating white working-class voters with rhetoric they perceive as hostile, has a genuine strategic opening if cost-of-living pressures worsen or the incumbent is perceived as indifferent to them."
